; Coldwater Ridge - a track for camber(1).
;
; This file is the whole course.  Nothing about it is compiled into the
; game: camber reads it at start-up, camber -e writes it, and a shell
; script can generate one, because it is text.
;
; The header is KEY VALUE lines.  After the % comes one feature a line:
;
;	X LANE FEATURE [SPEED]
;
; X is in tiles of eight logical pixels from the start line, LANE counts
; down from nought, and FEATURE is one of ramp, bump, mud, strip or
; rider.  SPEED is a rider's pace in hundredths of a pixel a frame and
; is ignored for everything else.

title Coldwater Ridge
length 200
lanes 4

%

; A row of strips to get everyone moving.
16 0 strip
16 1 strip
16 2 strip
16 3 strip

; Somebody is already ahead on the outside.
30 3 rider 180

26 1 bump
26 2 bump

; Ramps from here on, staggered, so the lane you pick decides when you
; are in the air and who you are next to when you land.
34 0 ramp
34 2 ramp
42 1 ramp
42 3 ramp

55 0 rider 200

52 0 mud
52 3 mud
60 1 bump
60 2 bump

; The first row that leaves no way round.
68 0 ramp
68 1 ramp
68 2 ramp
68 3 ramp

75 2 rider 170

78 1 strip
78 2 strip
86 1 mud
86 2 mud

98 1 rider 210

94 0 ramp
94 1 bump
94 2 ramp
94 3 bump
104 0 bump
104 1 ramp
104 2 bump
104 3 ramp

114 0 strip
114 3 strip

120 3 rider 190

; The whole width goes to mud.  There is no clean line through this, only
; a choice about whether to arrive at it hot.
122 0 mud
122 1 mud
122 2 mud
122 3 mud

132 1 ramp
132 2 ramp
140 0 bump
140 3 bump

145 2 rider 200

148 0 ramp
148 3 ramp
156 1 strip
156 2 strip

160 0 rider 175

; Last ramps, then the run-in.
164 0 ramp
164 1 ramp
164 2 ramp
164 3 ramp
174 0 bump
174 1 bump
174 2 bump
174 3 bump

178 1 rider 205

182 0 strip
182 1 strip
182 2 strip
182 3 strip
